# `railway up` uploads the working directory as the build context.
#
# Same reason as .dockerignore, different consumer: that command packages the
# local tree, and this tree carries a 209 GB `target/`. A CLI deploy without this
# file does not fail with a useful message — it sits there compressing a quarter
# of a terabyte and looks like a queued, stagnant deployment.
#
# Kept as a separate file rather than a symlink because the two tools read
# different formats in edge cases, and a broken symlink here would silently mean
# "exclude nothing".
#
# Before adding a pattern, read the WHAT MUST NOT BE EXCLUDED section in
# .dockerignore. `scripts/` in particular holds Rust [[bin]] sources that the
# Dockerfile builds by name, not just shell scripts.

target/
**/target/
.git/
docs/
*.pdf
.github/
.env
.env.*
avatars_cache/
static/rabble/
